@      *$SET TRACE ASMLIST COPYLIST PARAS REF
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID.   MPTZ007.
       AUTHOR.       PENNY GENOVESE.
       DATE-WRITTEN. FEBRUARY 26, 1992.
      *****************************************************************
      *SYSTEM NAME:   EDITORIAL SYSTEMS
      *APPL NAME:     OEM PARTS UPDATE
      *PROGRAM NAME:  MPTZ007 - OEM PARTS UPDATE REPORTING
      *LANGUAGE:      COBOL - Oracle
      *
      *DESCRIPTION: THIS PROGRAM PRODUCES THE OEM BATCH UPDATE REPORTS.
      *
      *  INPUT:    CONTROL INFORMATION (PROGRAM PARM FILE)
      *            Oracle OEM TABLE
      *
      *  I/O:      Oracle REPORT TABLE
      *
      *  OUTPUT:   MPTZ007-01  TRANSACTION ERROR REPORT
      *            MPTZ007-02  MULTIPLE SUPERSESSION DETAILS REPORT
      *            MPTZ007-03  PRICE UPDATE VARIANCE (CEG) REPORT
      *            MPTZ007-04  OEM BATCH UPDATE CONTROL REPORTS
      *            MPTZ007-05  ZERO-PRICED PARTS WITH LINES REPORTS
      *
      * SIGNIFICANT PROCESSING NARRATIVE:
      *            PROGRAM FETCHES ALL ROWS ASSOCIATED WITH EACH REPORT
      *            FROM THE Oracle TABLE ACQ_BATCH_REPORTS. (THESE ROWS
      *            WERE ENTERED VIA THE OEM PARTS UPDATE PROGRAMS.)
      *            AFTER ALL REPORTS ARE WRITTEN, THE ASSOCIATED Oracle
      *            ROWS ARE DELETED FROM THE TABLE.
      *
      * CALLED PROGRAMS:
      *            ILBOABNO - ABEND ROUTINE
      *     CALL "dberrmsg" USING SQLCA ERROR-MESSAGE ERROR-LENGTH.
      *
      * CONTROL CARD:
      *  (SAME CONTROL CARD THAT'S USED IN THE UPDATE PROGRAMS)
      *
      *  OEM=XXX,REGN=XX,EFFDT=XX/XX/XXXX,REPLACE=X,RUNTYP=XXX,
      *       1       2            3              4         5
      *
      *  NAGSTYP=XXXXXXXX
      *              6
      *
      *       1 - NUMERIC; OEM NUMBER WHICH YOU ARE PROCESSING
      *
      *       2 - ALPHA; REGION OF THE OEM
      *
      *       3 - NUMERIC; PRICE EFFECTIVE DATE AS SPECIFIED BY THE
      *           OEM  (FORMAT MM/DD/YYYY; MUST BE GREATER THAN LAST RUN
      *           UNLESS THIS IS REPLACEMENT RUN - THEN MUST = LAST RUN)
      *
      *       4 - ALPHA; REPLACEMENT INDICATOR (FOR PRICE UPDATE PGM);
      *           (N = NEW RUN, PRICES WILL BE UPDATED - CURRENT MOVED
      *           TO PREVIOUS THEN TRANSACTION PRICE MOVED TO CURRENT;
      *           Y = REPLACEMENT RUN, TRANSACTION PRICE MOVED DIRECTLY
      *           OVER CURRENT PRICE; USED FOR CORRECTING MISPRICING.)
      *
      *       5 - ALPHA; TYPE OF RUN (OEM = OEM, SUP = SUPPLIMENTAL)
      *           (USED BY REPORT PROGRAM MPTZ007)
      *
      *       6 - ALPHA; TYPE OF NAGS RUN (FOR NAGS RUN, EITHER "IMPORT"
      *           OR "DOMESTIC"; ANY OTHER RUNS, "N/A")
      *           (PRINTED IN HEADING - JUST TO DISTINGUISH BETWEEN THE
      *            IMPORT AND DOMESTIC RUN REPORTS)
      *
      *
      * MODIFICATION LOG:
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 10/25/2021  BY:   PENNY GENOVESE
      *             DESC: Changed creation of Price Variance from rpt to
      *                   pipe-delimitted file and omit service info.
